cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A counterexample to Liu's conjecture on Fano indices in dimension four"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/fuzzy-guacamole"
keywords:
  - Fano index
  - weighted projective space
  - Calabi-Yau variety
  - log canonical singularity
  - index
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  H. Liu conjectured that, in each dimension n >= 2, the Fano indices of
  canonical weighted projective n-spaces, the indices of terminal Calabi-Yau
  n-folds and the indices of n-dimensional log canonical singularities form
  the same set. We show that 1389 is the index of a terminal Calabi-Yau
  fourfold and of a four-dimensional log canonical singularity, and is not
  the Fano index of any canonical weighted projective fourspace. The
  non-membership is checked in the Lean 4 kernel.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "On Fano indices of weighted projective spaces"
    authors:
      - family-names: Liu
        given-names: Haidong
    year: 2026
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.03434"
    notes: "arXiv:2608.03434v3, Conjecture 4.2"
